<section class="wrap">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">6.1 to 6.5</p>
    <h2 id="t-where">Five Places the Same Surface Turns Up</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>In the cosmos <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>Galactic magnetic fields wind poloidally and toroidally through the disc and halo; accretion
        structures are tori; the jets of an active nucleus leave along the axis of one. A galaxy is not a
        disc with a hole so much as a circulation with an axis.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>In quantum mechanics <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>Orbital probability clouds with non-zero angular momentum are toroidal: the electron is not
        anywhere in particular, and the shape of where it is not is a ring around an axis of nodal
        silence.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>In fusion energy <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>Every tokamak ever built is a torus, and not for aesthetic reasons. Confining a plasma requires a
        field with no ends; a torus is the shape that lets the field close on itself without a boundary
        for the plasma to strike.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>In every neuron <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>Depolarisation travels out, the membrane repolarises, ions are pumped back, and the cell returns
        to a resting state ready to fire again. The cycle is a loop in state space that circulates and
        returns &mdash; the same topology, drawn in ion gradients.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="frame illuminated">
      <h3 id="t-life">In the shape of your life <span class="myth">&#9670;</span></h3>
      <p>You return to the same questions, the same rooms, the same arguments &mdash; and not at the same
        place, because the return happens one turn further along. That is the toroidal reading of a life:
        a circulation that comes back, displaced along the axis by everything accumulated in the loop.
        This is the point at which the geometry becomes a way of living rather than a way of calculating,
        and the site marks it as vision rather than as physics.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">✦</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Earned</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Tokamaks, toroidal orbitals, galactic field geometry and the neuronal cycle are all real and
          correctly described. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>A torus is the simplest orientable surface of genus one &mdash; the formal sense in which it
          both circulates and returns. <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="frame card">
      <h3>Chosen</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>That these instances share a <em>cause</em> rather than a constraint. Many systems are
          toroidal because toroids solve a boundary problem; that is an explanation the framework must
          out-argue, not ignore. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></li>
        <li>That the torus is &ldquo;π applied twice&rdquo; in any sense stronger than a figure of speech.
          <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

